                <pb facs="0115" n="83" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v01/pg83"/>

                <head>38. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On February 11, Radford sent a memorandum from the Joint Chiefs of Staff to the
                    Secretary of Defense recommending concepts and broad outline plans for the use
                    of United States military power under the Manila Pact in the event of Communist
                    aggression in Southeast Asia. For the text, see <hi rendition="#italic">United
                        States–Vietnam Relations, 1945–1967</hi>, Book 10, pages 885–887.</p>
            </div>
